        "text": "82"
      },
      {
        "y": 23.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 423.1,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Whatchamacallit: being indirect"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 237.1,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Vague and general words"
      },
      {
        "y": 88.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 508.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "In informal speech, we make frequent use of rather vague words and words with many different or"
      },
      {
        "y": 100,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 275.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "rather general meanings, like thing or get."
      },
      {
        "y": 112,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 379.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "That’s one of the things I want to talk to him about. [thing = subject]"
      },
      {
        "y": 124,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 391.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Laura has got a thing about mice. [she either really likes or dislikes them]"
      },
      {
        "y": 136,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 378.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Don’t make such a big thing of it! [Don’t make so much fuss about it!]"
      },
      {
        "y": 148,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 354.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "There wasn’t a thing we could do about it. [a thing = anything]"
      },
      {
        "y": 160,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 475,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "For one thing, I haven’t got time. For another thing, I can’t afford it. [Firstly …, secondly …]"
      },
      {
        "y": 172,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 493.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The thing is, I have to take my car for a service tomorrow morning. [used to introduce a topic or a"
      },
      {
        "y": 185.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 244.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "problem, or to provide an explanation]"
      },
      {
        "y": 196,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 288.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "As things are at present, … [as the situation is]"
      },
      {
        "y": 208,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 276.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I don’t get what you’re saying. [understand]"
      },
      {
        "y": 220,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 299.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "We must get that parcel in the post today. [send]"
      },
      {
        "y": 232,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 486.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "She had big plans to travel the world but she just never got it together. [took positive action or"
      },
      {
        "y": 245.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 167.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "organised herself]"
      },
      {
        "y": 256,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 434.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Jill will get things sorted (out) today. [organise things so that the problem is solved]"
      },
      {
        "y": 268,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 352.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I hope I can get her to myself this evening. [be alone with her]"
      },
      {
        "y": 289.3,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 282.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B When you can’t think of the word"
      },
      {
        "y": 307.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 437,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "When we can’t remember a word or name, we often replace it with a vague word."
      },
      {
        "y": 318.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "For objects: thingy, thingummy /ˈθɪŋəmi/, thingumijig /ˈθɪŋəmədʒɪg/, thingamibob /ˈθɪŋəməbɒb/,"
      },
      {
        "y": 330.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 330.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "whatsit, whatchamacallit /ˈwɒtʃəməˌkɔːlɪt/, whatnot"
      },
      {
        "y": 342.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 352.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Have you seen the thingy we use for keeping the door open?"
      },
      {
        "y": 354.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 503.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "For people: whatsisname /ˈwɒtsɪzneɪm/ (for a man); whatsername /ˈwɒtsəneɪm/ (for a woman)"
      },
      {
        "y": 366.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 238.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Did you see whatsisname today?"
      },
      {
        "y": 378.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Note that these words can be written in different ways. It is also possible to use thingy for either a"
      },
      {
        "y": 390.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 359.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "man or a woman: I was talking to thingy about that yesterday."
      },
      {
        "y": 410.8,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 161.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Quantifiers"
      },
      {
        "y": 428.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Some quantifiers are common in informal speaking but are rare in formal writing. For example, the"
      },
      {
        "y": 440.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 248.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "following expressions mean a lot of:"
      },
      {
        "y": 456.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 465.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "bags of a load of loads of a mass of masses of dozens of tons of umpteen"
      },
      {
        "y": 471.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 254.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I can help you – I’ve got bags of time."
      },
      {
        "y": 483.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 412.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "They can afford to go on expensive holidays as they’ve got loads of money."
      },
      {
        "y": 495.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 437.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I’ve tried phoning her umpteen times but she never seems to answer her mobile."
      },
      {
        "y": 507.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 351.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "These expressions mean a little or some: a bit of, a scrap of."
      },
      {
        "y": 519.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 215.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I’ve got a bit of a headache."
      },
      {
        "y": 531.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 393.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You’ve been sitting there all day but you haven’t done a scrap of work."
      },
      {
        "y": 551.2,
        "x0": 74.4,
        "x1": 291.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "D Being indirect and less threatening"
      },
      {
        "y": 569.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 493.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Here are some expressions which we can use in speech to make what we are saying sound less"
      },
      {
        "y": 581.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 385.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "threatening and potentially offensive to the person we are talking to."
      },
      {
        "y": 592.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "It’s not the most practical/sensible/intelligent/appropriate thing you’ve ever done. [it’s impractical /"
      },
      {
        "y": 606.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 304.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "not very sensible / rather unintelligent / inappropriate]"
      },
      {
        "y": 616.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 420.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "It’s not the most practical idea – and I mean that in the nicest possible way."
      },
      {
        "y": 628.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 411.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "No offence intended, but I think you’ve misunderstood the basic problem."
      },
      {
        "y": 640.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 452.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If you don’t mind me/my saying so, I think that you could have handled that better."
      },
      {
        "y": 652.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 450.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I gather you feel upset by the recent changes in the office. [I’ve heard it from someone]"
      },
      {
        "y": 664.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Incidentally, have you paid your money for the club outing yet? [often used to introduce a new subject"
      },
      {
        "y": 678.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 250.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "into the conversation in an indirect way]"
      },
      {
        "y": 688.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 454.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "What a load of idiots – present company excepted, of course. [not including you or me]"
      },
      {
        "y": 700.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 447.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The staff here, myself included, have not been working quite as hard as we should."
      }
    ],
